bug_report:
[modules] export using of purview 'extern "C++"' declaration not bound in importers
Consider:

  // a.cpp
  export module M;
  extern "C++" void foo();
  export using ::foo;

  // b.cpp
  import M;
  int main() { foo(); }

$ g++ -fmodules -S a.cpp b.cpp
b.cpp: In function ‘int main()’:
b.cpp:2:14: error: ‘foo’ was not declared in this scope
    2 | int main() { foo(); }
      |              ^~~

Note that this works if 'foo' had been defined in the GMF instead of within the module purview.
